R(341,"B","resilient","Network identity","An ENI retains its MAC address and can preserve network identity when moved to a replacement instance in the same AZ.",
"An arbitrary OS-assigned spoofed MAC is not the supported way to preserve EC2 interface identity.|A detachable secondary ENI preserves its assigned MAC/IP attributes for a same-AZ replacement.|Private subnet placement does not itself preserve one specific interface's identity across new instances.|A subnet has an address range; it is not a per-application persistent MAC identity.","eni", "Use an appropriate secondary ENI, preserve it on termination and plan same-AZ attachment. ENIs cannot move across AZs, and the application must bind licensing to that interface.")
R(342,"D","performance","IP address planning","Associate a non-overlapping secondary VPC CIDR and create additional subnets without replacing the VPC.",
"Subnets cannot simply be resized in place, and deleting occupied subnets is disruptive.|A replacement VPC is unnecessary when secondary address space can meet the requirement.|A peered new VPC creates another network and dependency migration rather than expanding the existing one.|A secondary CIDR adds address space while preserving the original VPC and its existing resources.","subnet vpc", "Check CIDR-association quotas, overlap/routing restrictions and downstream routes/firewalls before using the new space.")
h(343,"The question only asks to 'enhance customer service'. Polly, Lex, Kendra and Textract can all support legitimate customer-service workflows, and it gives no workload constraints that select exactly TWO.","performance","AI service selection","reko translate")
REVIEWS[344] = dict(REVIEWS[269])
R(345,"B","cost","Object version lifecycle","Deleting a key in a versioned bucket normally creates a delete marker while retained object versions continue to incur storage charges.",
"A key-only DELETE does not permanently remove the current data version; it normally adds a marker.|The marker hides the current key but old versions remain stored until explicitly removed or expired.|S3 versioning is not a fixed thirty-day recycle-bin service.|Authorized API/CLI requests with version IDs can permanently delete versions; the console is not mandatory.","versioning")
h(346,"A Lambda can construct a usable download/presigned link and send it through SES. A native S3-to-SNS email notification instead contains an event record and does not generate the requested usable download link for external recipients. Only one complete option is supplied despite Select TWO.","resilient","Event notifications","s3events presign")
R(347,"B","resilient","Container bootstrap","Host daemon and ECS agent settings belong in the container instance's bootstrap, not in a task's application definition.",
"Cluster metadata does not execute host operating-system/bootstrap configuration.|EC2 user data can write daemon/agent configuration and join the desired cluster at boot.|Task definitions describe application containers and task settings rather than arbitrary host daemon setup.|Service definitions manage task deployment/count and do not bootstrap each host OS.","userdata ecs")
R(348,"B","secure","Audit & observability","CloudTrail records supported management API events with identity, time, source address and request context.",
"EventBridge can route API-derived events, but it is not the authoritative retained API audit service by itself.|CloudTrail management-event records show CreateCluster actors, event times, source IPs and request parameters.|Aggregate CloudWatch metrics do not identify who called a resource-creation API.|Trusted Advisor recommendations are not a resource-creation identity audit history.","audit", "For historical cross-account/Region queries, configure organization trails and an appropriate retained query solution; default Event History is time/Region limited.")
R(349,"ABD","resilient","API integrations","API Gateway supports HTTP endpoints, authorized cross-account Lambda integrations and private integrations through VPC Links.",
"HTTP/HTTP_PROXY integrations can forward supported requests to public HTTP backends.|Cross-account Lambda integration is supported with the required function resource policy and integration configuration.|A raw database wire-protocol session is not an ordinary API Gateway backend integration type.|A VPC Link connects supported API configurations to private backend resources without public exposure.|SFTP is not a native request/response backend integration protocol for API Gateway.","privateapi apigw")
R(350,"D","performance","API caching","Include the request's asset/category selector as a cache-key parameter to separate representations in one stage.",
"Compression changes payload size, not the logical request fields used as cache keys.|A custom domain changes API addressing rather than partitioning the cache by requested asset class.|Separate stages could separate caches but duplicate the environment the question asks to keep unified.|A configured query-string cache-key parameter creates distinct entries for equity and fixed-income requests.","apicache", "Define/invalidate the appropriate key entries and avoid caching user-specific responses under shared keys.")
R(351,"A","performance","Machine learning platforms","SageMaker AI provides a managed lifecycle for preparing data, training/tuning custom models and deploying supported inference endpoints.",
"SageMaker's model-development, AutoML/training and deployment capabilities fit a custom churn model.|Lex builds conversational interfaces rather than an arbitrary churn-model training pipeline.|Polly synthesizes speech rather than training prediction models on customer features.|Comprehend focuses on managed text analysis, not this general mixed-feature model lifecycle.","sagemaker", "Feature choices depend on model/framework and endpoint type; serverless endpoints do not support every model or inference capability.")
R(352,"ADE","performance","Edge request processing","Lambda@Edge has viewer-request/response and origin-request/response triggers; only three real trigger names appear in these options.",
"Viewer Request executes on supported incoming viewer-request events.|CloudFront Cache is not the name of a Lambda@Edge trigger hook.|Sender Request is not a defined Lambda@Edge event type.|Origin Request executes when CloudFront sends the request toward the origin.|Origin Response executes when CloudFront receives the origin's response.","edge", "Viewer Response is a fourth supported trigger, but it is not one of the choices.")
R(353,"D","resilient","Function deployments","A Lambda code update has a propagation period during which invocations can continue on the previous code; version/alias deployment controls make transitions explicit.",
"Lambda does not impose a universal five-minute request queue while updating code.|Updating code does not require a separate general enable operation before it can serve requests.|Code need not embed a version number to accept invocations; versions and aliases are invocation/deployment controls.|During update propagation, invocations can observe old versus newly deployed code rather than an instantaneous global cutover.","lambdaUpdate", "The screenshot's '<1 minute' wording is not an SLA. Publish immutable versions and use aliases/controlled traffic shifting when release consistency matters.")
R(354,"BCD","resilient","Serverless event sources","Event source mappings are managed pollers for supported queues/streams; SNS invokes Lambda directly through a subscription instead.",
"SNS is a push integration and does not use a Lambda polling event source mapping.|Kinesis Data Streams is a supported poll-based stream event source.|SQS queues are supported poll-based event source mappings.|DynamoDB Streams supplies the change records consumed through an event source mapping.|CodePipeline invocation/action integrations are not this native queue/stream poller mechanism.","esm")
FIXES[355] = {"options": ["Use AWS Trusted Advisor to analyze your AWS environment.", "Use AWS CloudTrail and review the event history of your AWS account.", "Use AWS Config to set up a rule in your AWS account.", "Use AWS IAM to generate a credential report."]}
R(355,"C","secure","Configuration compliance","Config records supported resource configurations and evaluates rules such as S3 public-access compliance checks.",
"Trusted Advisor offers checks/recommendations but not the full supported-resource configuration history/evaluation workflow requested.|CloudTrail audits API calls, not the managed current-state compliance evaluation of bucket configurations.|Config configuration recording plus appropriate managed/custom rules detects relevant S3 configuration changes and noncompliance.|IAM credential reports describe IAM credential status rather than S3 bucket configuration/public access.","config")
MERGES[356] = [357]
FIXES[356] = {"options": ["Use a combination of SNS to buffer requests and process them asynchronously using On-Demand EC2 instances.", "Replace Kinesis Data Streams with an SQS queue and create a Lambda function to process requests asynchronously.", "Use SQS to queue requests and process them asynchronously using On-Demand EC2 instances.", "Use Lambda and Step Functions to orchestrate service components and process requests asynchronously."]}
R(356,"B","cost","Asynchronous processing","A low-volume five-minute task can run in Lambda from an SQS work queue without idle EC2 workers or unnecessary workflow transitions.",
"SNS alone is not a durable worker queue, and an always provisioned EC2 worker adds idle cost.|SQS buffers pending work and a Lambda event source mapping processes bounded tasks on demand.|EC2 workers can work but retain host provisioning/idle overhead for a small sporadic workload.|Step Functions adds orchestration cost/complexity when the described work can be handled as one queued task.","sqs lambda", "Use small object references rather than image bodies in messages; upload to S3 and report asynchronous job status through an application mechanism. The HTTP request should not remain open for the five-minute job.")
FIXES[358] = {"options": ["Use Amazon GuardDuty to monitor malicious activity on S3.", "Use Amazon Rekognition to monitor and recognize access patterns on S3.", "Use Amazon Inspector to alert whenever a security violation is detected on S3.", "Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor and detect access patterns on S3."]}
R(358,"A","secure","Threat detection","GuardDuty S3 Protection analyzes supported S3 activity for suspicious behavior; auditing and visual recognition are different functions.",
"Enable GuardDuty and applicable S3 Protection findings for suspicious API/data-access behavior.|Rekognition analyzes visual content; it is not an S3 identity/access threat detector.|Inspector assesses supported workload vulnerabilities rather than suspicious S3 object-access patterns.|CloudTrail records access events but needs detection/analysis logic; GuardDuty supplies the managed threat detection here.","guardduty audit", "GuardDuty does not by itself enforce every compliance setting; use Config/IAM controls for configuration compliance. Screenshot quiz/navigation artifacts were removed from the extracted options.")
h(359,"The historical offline-transfer answer is Snowball devices, but new-customer Snowball access ended in November 2025 and Snowmobile is retired. The question omits eligibility, required completion time and current transfer alternatives, so its fastest/cheapest claim is not a current general recommendation.","cost","Bulk migration","datasync")
MERGES[360] = [361]
FIXES[360] = {"options": ["Install the CloudWatch agent on each instance and monitor the SwapUtilization metric.", "Create a CloudWatch dashboard and monitor the SwapUsed metric.", "Enable detailed monitoring on each instance and monitor the SwapUtilization metric.", "Create a CloudTrail trail and configure CloudWatch Logs to monitor the trail logs."]}
R(360,"A","resilient","Host observability","Guest swap usage needs an OS-level agent/custom metric; default EC2 infrastructure metrics do not collect it.",
"The CloudWatch agent can collect the relevant guest swap usage counters on each supported host.|A dashboard cannot visualize guest counters that have never been collected/published.|Detailed EC2 monitoring changes frequency of built-in metrics; it does not add guest swap measurements.|CloudTrail audit events do not measure an instance's swap usage.","cwmetrics", "SwapUtilization/SwapUsed are source shorthand, not universal unified-agent names. Linux agent metrics include swap_used, swap_free and swap_used_percent; Windows uses the configured performance counter.")
R(362,"D","secure","Immutable object storage","DataSync moves existing file data to S3; Object Lock retention protects object versions against overwrite/deletion for the configured period.",
"A continuously deployed hybrid gateway is unnecessary for a one-time migration followed by cloud storage and needs a compatible retention design.|EBS does not have an S3 Object Lock feature; block storage is the wrong retention interface.|EFS does not implement S3 Object Lock on its files.|DataSync supplies managed migration and S3 supplies Object Lock; configure an actual retention/legal-hold policy.","datasync objectlock", "Object Lock enabling alone is not indefinite protection: define retention/hold and use compliance mode where governance bypass is unacceptable.")
R(363,"B","secure","Endpoint authorization","An endpoint policy restricts which S3 resources/actions may be reached through that gateway endpoint.",
"A bucket policy can restrict a bucket's callers/path but does not configure which bucket resources this endpoint permits.|The S3 gateway endpoint's policy can scope allowed operations to the trusted bucket/object ARNs.|An endpoint policy is configured on an endpoint, not generated as a policy of trusted VPC objects.|A bucket policy is resource-side authorization; the question specifically asks to restrict access through the gateway endpoint.","s3endpoint", "Endpoint policies supplement IAM/bucket permissions and do not grant access by themselves.")
R(364,"B","resilient","Queue prioritization","SQS does not have a per-message priority field; use separate queues and a worker scheduling policy.",
"SQS does not automatically process a higher arbitrary message-priority attribute first.|Separate premium/free queues let workers poll and allocate capacity to premium work first.|S3 stores images but does not implement queue processing priority.|Kinesis streaming is not a direct priority scheduling fix for the two service tiers.","sqs", "Prevent indefinite starvation of free users with explicit scheduling/capacity shares if necessary.")
R(365,"A","secure","Private database access","Use a DynamoDB gateway endpoint for applicable VPC-to-DynamoDB API traffic and AWS Backup for supported cross-account retained backups.",
"A gateway endpoint supplies local DynamoDB routing; AWS Backup provides scheduled retained recovery points and supported cross-account copies.|DynamoDB's ordinary VPC integration is not the described interface-endpoint route-table mechanism, and PITR is not a cross-account backup-copy plan.|Timestream does not provide another account's DynamoDB point-in-time restore capability.|NACL rules do not target DNS names/gateway endpoint objects, and built-in on-demand backup alone is not this cross-account automation.","s3endpoint backup", "DAX endpoints are already private VPC endpoints for cache access. Advanced DynamoDB backup features, Organizations policies, destination vault/key permissions and supported Regions must be configured for cross-account copies.")
R(366,"AE","secure","Workforce identity","Organizations consolidates accounts; IAM Identity Center with an AD-backed identity source supplies workforce access.",
"Create the organization and invite eligible accounts to establish the managed multi-account structure.|SCPs constrain permissions but do not establish workforce sign-in; this is less complete than the explicit Identity Center/AD Connector setup in E.|Organizations has no generic external-authentication toggle that replaces configuring an Identity Center identity source.|Cognito identity pools are an application credential mechanism, not this standard Identity Center workforce directory integration.|Identity Center can use the supported Directory Service/AD Connector setup to federate the existing corporate directory.","orgbilling identitycenter")
R(367,"D","resilient","Backup automation","Data Lifecycle Manager schedules and retains tag-targeted EBS snapshots without custom scheduler hosts.",
"Storage Gateway is not the native snapshot scheduler for EC2 EBS volumes.|A CLI cron job adds custom scheduling, retry and retention management.|S3 Lifecycle manages bucket objects, not EBS snapshot creation.|DLM automates EBS snapshot schedules and lifecycle policies for selected supported volumes/instances.","dlm backup")
R(368,"A","secure","Temporary credentials","STS issues temporary AWS credentials for role sessions; Cognito JWTs are not the same AWS access-key/session-token credential set.",
"STS AssumeRole can issue short-lived AWS credentials for a production role with the required scoped permissions.|The options have distinct functions; a JWT token alone does not replace STS role credentials.|Cognito user-pool JWTs authenticate application users rather than directly supply the specified AWS API credential tuple.|Identity Center provides workforce access and uses roles/temporary sessions, but STS is the credential-issuing service asked for.","iam identitycenter")
R(369,"A","secure","Immutable object retention","Object Lock compliance retention protects versions; a lifecycle rule can later transition retained data to Deep Archive.",
"S3 Object Lock requires versioning; configure at least the required compliance retention and a later archive transition.|Versioning without Object Lock allows authorized permanent deletion and One Zone-IA has different AZ-loss properties.|Ordinary versioning preserves history but does not enforce immutable three-year retention.|Governance mode has authorized bypass and the option does not include the requested archive transition.","objectlock s3", "Retention starts with each protected object version; enabling Object Lock alone does not set a three-year retention rule.")
R(370,"DE","cost","Static content delivery","S3 stores static objects durably; CloudFront caches them globally and supports restricted viewer/origin access.",
"Global Accelerator is not a cache or direct substitute for CloudFront delivery from S3.|Lambda compute is not required merely to store and distribute static media.|Fargate tasks add unnecessary server/container processing for static-object delivery.|S3 provides the durable object origin without running file-serving hosts.|CloudFront provides global edge caching and supported private-content authorization controls.","s3 cloudfront")
R(371,"BD","resilient","Block storage characteristics","EBS is persistent AZ-scoped block storage; supported Elastic Volumes changes can be performed on attached volumes.",
"EBS snapshots are not stored in customer RDS databases; that service attribution is incorrect.|EBS data can persist independently of the attached instance, subject to configured deletion-on-termination.|Volume redundancy is within its AZ, not automatic cross-Region replication.|Supported Elastic Volumes modifications change type/size/performance while attached, with documented constraints and filesystem follow-up.|An EBS volume attaches within its own AZ; cross-AZ use requires copying/restoring the data.","ebs", "Persistent volume storage is not a reason to put every workload on EBS; choose storage based on each workload's actual interface, availability and performance needs.")
R(372,"AE","secure","Network troubleshooting","Same-VPC connectivity uses local routes plus permitted SG/NACL traffic; it does not require public internet routing or identical instance classes.",
"Allow the application-to-database port/protocol through the relevant security groups.|Instance class equality is not a condition for ordinary IP connectivity.|Placement groups optimize hardware placement, not permission to communicate across subnets.|An internet/NAT default route is not required for direct local VPC traffic.|NACLs are stateless, so permit both the application flow and required return traffic across the subnets.","vpc")
R(373,"CD","resilient","Hybrid network availability","Add an independent Direct Connect path or a VPN directly to the target VPC; peering does not transit another VPC's hybrid gateway.",
"VPN CloudHub is not a service that provisions the asserted Direct Connect path.|A connection to VPC-2 does not automatically provide transitive gateway access to peered VPC-1.|A second independently designed connection to VPC-1 removes dependence on a single Direct Connect path.|An internet VPN directly to VPC-1 supplies an alternative transport if the Direct Connect path fails.|A VPN terminating only in VPC-2 cannot be transitively used through ordinary VPC peering to reach VPC-1.","vpn peering", "Use diverse physical locations/devices/providers for real redundancy and test BGP/route preference; merely ordering another same-location circuit is not complete fault isolation.")

R(374,"D","secure","Workload IAM roles","Use an EC2 instance role/profile for automatically managed temporary AWS credentials.",
"Security groups filter packets; they do not store or issue AWS API credentials.|Static credentials on the instance introduce rotation/exposure problems.|A bastion is not a credential-distribution service for application API calls.|An appropriately scoped instance role supplies temporary credentials that supported SDKs obtain automatically.","iam")
R(375,"D","performance","Edge response customization","Edge request logic can select an existing image variant and control headers; cache variants must be keyed correctly.",
"Route 53 cannot inspect an HTTP User-Agent header to choose a distribution.|An EC2 conversion service adds host operations when suitable variants/edge routing can meet the request.|A response headers policy sets headers; it does not dynamically convert/select image bytes based on User-Agent.|Use supported edge logic to rewrite/select the format path and modify headers, with appropriate caching.","edge", "CloudFront cache behaviors match paths, not arbitrary User-Agent conditions. Lambda@Edge must perform the conditional selection, normally using Accept/capability data and pre-generated/origin-generated variants; it is not an automatic built-in image converter.")
R(376,"C","secure","Remote administration","A public Windows bastion with corporate-source-restricted RDP centralizes administration of private Windows instances.",
"Global SSH ingress does not implement restricted RDP access to a Windows bastion.|The corporate network is not connected to the VPC, so placing the bastion there alone does not establish access.|A public bastion can accept RDP only from trusted corporate public addresses and relay authorized access to private hosts.|A private-subnet host is not directly reachable from the internet merely by associating an Elastic IP.","vpc sessionmanager", "Restrict target RDP to the bastion SG and harden/audit sessions. Session Manager is an alternative when the jump-host requirement can change.")
R(377,"BE","performance","Static website DNS","Direct S3 website-domain routing requires a matching bucket name and control of the registered domain; Route 53 hosted zones are global.",
"MX records route email, not an HTTP static website.|The bucket name must match the domain used for direct S3 website routing.|Hosted zones are not regional resources that must share the bucket's Region.|CORS addresses cross-origin browser API requests, not ordinary DNS routing to a site.|A registered/control-authorized domain is needed to delegate and publish the website DNS records.","dns", "Use the appropriate S3 website endpoint and alias record. CloudFront in front of S3 supports HTTPS and changes the direct-domain naming constraints.")
R(378,"C","cost","Archive migration","DataSync can deliver directly into S3 Deep Archive; a mandatory thirty-day Standard staging period is not required.",
"Standard then a transition works but incurs an unnecessary initial hot-storage period for the stated cold records.|Storage Gateway is an ongoing hybrid access interface, not the lowest-operations one-time migration tool here.|DataSync supports selecting Deep Archive as the destination class for suitable cold data.|The proposal mixes gateway/archive interfaces and an unnecessary staged lifecycle instead of a direct managed migration.","datasyncS3", "Validate data verification options, retrieval SLA, minimum archive duration and small-object metadata overhead before selecting the destination class.")
R(379,"A","resilient","DNS failover","Use health-aware primary/secondary failover records for a warm-standby regional application.",
"Failover routing selects the secondary when the configured primary health evaluation fails.|Weighted routing ordinarily splits queries rather than keeping a zero-traffic standby until failure.|A custom API-driven record updater is unnecessary when native health-aware routing meets the requirement.|An alarm/Lambda DNS mutation workflow adds operations and race/failback handling compared with native failover.","routing dr", "Health checks must reach the monitored endpoint; Evaluate Target Health applies to supported aliases. DNS caches still affect client recovery time.")
R(380,"D","performance","DNS & routing","Geolocation routing maps geographic query locations to selected regional records.",
"An ALB is regional and does not automatically steer all global users to a country-selected Region.|Geo restriction allows/blocks CloudFront viewers; it does not map each country to the stated application Region.|Weights express proportions rather than location-specific country selection.|Geolocation records can map Japanese and Swedish queries to the intended endpoints.","routing", "DNS-location behavior depends on resolver/EDNS context; it is not by itself a legal data-residency or physical-user-location guarantee.")
R(381,"BD","resilient","Managed APIs","API Gateway provides managed REST/HTTP/WebSocket APIs; static anycast addresses and OS-bypass networking are different services.",
"Static anycast ingress addresses describe Global Accelerator, not API Gateway's general API endpoint capability.|API Gateway supports managed REST and WebSocket APIs integrated with serverless backends.|OS-bypass HPC networking describes EFA, not an API management service.|Usage-based API request/data-transfer charges describe the basic pricing model among these choices.|GraphQL is not automatically generated for arbitrary APIs; AppSync is the purpose-built managed GraphQL service.","apigw appsync", "Pricing also varies with API type and enabled features such as caching, private endpoints, WebSocket messages/connections and transfer.")
R(382,"D","secure","Private content moderation","Use Rekognition moderation through an interface endpoint for privately routed API requests from the VPC.",
"Custom SageMaker training adds model operations, and GuardDuty is not the component that makes the model API path private.|Monitron monitors industrial equipment, not general image moderation; TGW Network Manager is not a public-egress blocker.|Detective investigates security activity and Audit Manager gathers evidence; neither supplies the proposed image/private-routing features.|Rekognition detects supported moderation categories and PrivateLink supplies a privately addressed service API path.","reko privatelink", "Configure endpoint security/DNS/IAM policies and any required private S3 access separately; an interface endpoint does not force every other workload connection private.")
R(383,"CE","performance","Compute scaling","The default simple-scaling cooldown is 300 seconds; it gives applicable scaling activity time to affect metrics.",
"Cooldown does not guarantee zero downtime from instance launch/termination.|Six hundred seconds is not the documented default group cooldown.|For applicable simple policies, cooldown limits repeated adjustments before prior scaling has taken effect.|The purpose is policy stabilization, not physically cooling an instance before scale-out.|The default group cooldown is 300 seconds unless configured otherwise.","cooldown", "Cooldown behavior is policy/action specific; target tracking and step scaling use instance warm-up differently.")
R(384,"BD","resilient","Monitoring & alerting","CloudWatch evaluates metric thresholds and SNS delivers the resulting email notifications.",
"SES sends email but is not the native threshold-monitoring/notification pair required.|SNS sends alarm notifications to confirmed email subscriptions.|BIND serves DNS, not database performance alarms.|CloudWatch supplies database metrics and alarms tied to the desired threshold.|SQS is a work queue rather than a direct email notification channel.","cloudwatch sns")
R(385,"C","secure","Container task permissions","Application API permissions belong in the ECS task role, referenced by taskRoleArn.",
"Firehose is a delivery stream rather than a task queue, and taskDefinitionArn is not the task-role field.|AppStream is application streaming, not the specified message queue service.|An SQS queue fits the work pattern; taskRoleArn supplies scoped S3/SQS permissions to the application containers.|The claimed EnableTaskIAMRole task-definition setting is not how ECS assigns the application role.","taskrole sqs", "The task execution role is a separate role for agent-level actions such as pulling images/logging. Scope different task roles to the producer/consumer needs.")
h(386,"Adding a larger IPv4 subnet can work only if free VPC address space exists; IPv6-only subnets require supported instance/workload configurations. The source does not establish these prerequisites and incorrectly describes associating a new VPC, so it cannot uniquely choose the proposed migration path.","performance","IP address planning","subnet")
R(387,"B","performance","Application load balancing","ALB supports host/path rules and gRPC target protocol versions; NLB/GWLB do not provide the same HTTP routing rules.",
"UDP routing does not provide ALB host/path inspection or the specified gRPC integration.|Use ALB rules and supported HTTPS/gRPC target-group protocol configuration.|GWLB transparently distributes appliance traffic using GENEVE, not application host/path routing.|An NLB plus accelerator can improve transport reachability but does not supply the required HTTP host/path rules.","grpc alb")
REVIEWS[388] = dict(REVIEWS[337])
R(389,"B","resilient","Database failover","RDS changes the managed DB endpoint's DNS target to the standby during supported Multi-AZ failover; clients must reconnect.",
"A standby already exists for the traditional Multi-AZ instance deployment; creating one from scratch is not the normal failover step.|The endpoint name stays stable while its DNS target resolves to the promoted standby.|It is not a customer-managed reassignment of the old host's IP address to another AZ.|Rebooting the failed primary is not the availability mechanism that promotes the standby.","rds", "Refresh connections and honor DNS TTLs; failover is not zero-duration or a guarantee existing TCP sessions survive.")
R(390,"D","cost","Static website delivery","Static HTML/CSS/JS and images can be stored on S3 and distributed from CloudFront without paying for application server hosts.",
"Beanstalk adds application-server infrastructure unnecessary for a purely static website.|An EC2 Nginx host adds patching/capacity expense unnecessary for static assets.|An ASG/EBS server fleet and accelerator add compute without the CDN object-cache advantages needed.|S3 stores all static assets and CloudFront provides scalable edge caching close to viewers.","s3 cloudfront", "Point the public domain to CloudFront with the appropriate TLS certificate. For a private origin, use the S3 REST endpoint plus OAC instead of the website endpoint.")
R(391,"AB","performance","Horizontal scaling","Distributing traffic over additional instances increases capacity; only the two listed traffic-distribution choices provide that baseline.",
"Two endpoint records with weights can distribute DNS queries over more than one server.|An ELB distributes requests across registered healthy instances and supports later Auto Scaling integration.|WAF filters requests and is not an additional compute-capacity or traffic-distribution layer behind one instance.|There is no generic S3 Cache that turns the single dynamic EC2 application into a scaled tier.|Glue is data integration and does not supply web-tier load balancing or autoscaling.","alb routing", "These choices establish a multi-instance baseline, not complete automatic elasticity. Add an Auto Scaling group/policy when automatic capacity changes are required.")
h(392,"The offered 'minimum' topology misstates ALB public-subnet requirements and calls FQDNs a source identity for incoming requests. Network Firewall domain inspection applies to supported HTTP Host/TLS SNI flows, not authenticated source FQDN identity; NAT and a direct ALB integration do not solve this. A precise inspectable traffic direction/topology is required.","secure","Network inspection","vpc waf")
h(393,"The original PNG is a tiny horizontal strip with no readable question or answer content. This is a source attachment, not a recoverable exam question; no answer is inferred.","resilient","Unreadable source","dr")
MERGES[394] = [395]
R(394,"D","performance","Global download acceleration","CloudFront caches frequently reused software files at edge locations; disable-caching policies defeat that reuse.",
"Global Accelerator is not a direct S3 bucket download-cache endpoint and private VIFs do not appear automatically in remote locations.|CachingDisabled prevents edge reuse and adds a secondary origin without addressing the main repeated-download latency.|Transfer Acceleration can help distant transfers, but lacks the repeated-object edge cache of the direct CDN choice.|A CloudFront S3 origin with signed URLs delivers reusable private update files near remote clients.","cloudfront transferaccel", "The servers still need connectivity and authorized signed requests; benchmark cacheability and TTLs for release artifacts.")
R(396,"AD","resilient","Database failover","A failure affecting the active primary can trigger Multi-AZ failover; a failed replica/standby is repaired without deliberately failing healthy primary service to it.",
"Primary storage failure is a supported failure condition for promoting a healthy standby.|An independent read replica failure does not require switching the healthy primary.|A failed secondary is not a healthy candidate to promote in place of the running primary.|Loss of the primary AZ can trigger promotion of a healthy standby in another AZ.|Secondary storage failure calls for secondary recovery/replacement rather than promotion of that failed standby.","rds")
R(397,"A","performance","Data transformation","Glue crawlers catalog data and managed ETL jobs can convert CSV into Parquet without running a permanent custom processing cluster.",
"A crawler plus scheduled Glue ETL supplies managed schema discovery and the required conversion/output workflow.|A Lambda/EMR cluster chain adds custom provisioning/invocation operations for an ETL capability Glue supplies.|A Bash job definition alone does not implement a CSV-to-Parquet engine or automatic upload event triggers.|EMRFS is a filesystem layer, not a new-object discovery/scheduling service; the proposal omits orchestration.","glue")
R(398,"A","resilient","Stable private addressing","A secondary ENI can preserve a private service address when moved to a compatible replacement instance in the same AZ.",
"Use a secondary ENI retained beyond instance termination and reattach it to the same-AZ standby.|An attached primary ENI cannot be freely detached/moved this way, and Network Firewall does not provide that function.|An EIP is public addressing, while Transit Gateway does not automate EIP instance failover.|Transfer Family FTPS does not move EC2 network interfaces or change source/destination checking.","eni", "ENIs are AZ-scoped. This design does not survive an AZ failure and needs reliable failure detection/reattachment automation.")
R(399,"D","secure","Secret rotation","Secrets Manager supports encrypted application secret storage and configured rotation; Parameter Store SecureString alone does not automatically rotate credentials.",
"ACM manages certificates, not general database/API-password secrets.|SecureString encrypts values but does not automatically rotate arbitrary database/API credentials by default.|KMS protects keys and data-key operations; it is not the application secret-value/rotation registry.|Secrets Manager stores encrypted secret versions and supports appropriate managed/custom rotation workflows.","secrets", "Applications must refresh credentials from the current secret stage. Rotation support/connectivity and database availability need explicit setup.")
R(400,"D","resilient","Message filtering","SNS subscription filter policies route only matching messages to each SQS consumer queue.",
"Sending everything to every queue and filtering later wastes delivery/worker effort.|A Kinesis consumer router requires custom stream-processing code for a native SNS filter use case.|Multiple topics can route work but add topic/producer management that one filtered topic avoids.|One topic with per-subscription filters selects the intended quote queue before delivery.","sns sqs", "Configure queue retention and processing/retry deadlines separately; filtering does not impose a twenty-four-hour processing guarantee.")
R(401,"C","performance","Database selection","DynamoDB stores key-value/document items for designed keyed lookups, unlike relational warehouses or document collaboration products.",
"RDS provides relational tables, not the most direct key-value/document service choice.|Aurora Serverless scales relational compute but retains a relational data model.|DynamoDB supports flexible document items and scalable key-based access to the music metadata.|WorkDocs is not an operational application document database and its service availability must also be checked.","dynamo")
R(402,"C","secure","Web attack mitigation","Use CloudFront edge distribution with WAF rate-based controls on the supported web ingress.",
"Security groups do not have explicit deny rules, so the proposed security-group deny list is invalid.|GuardDuty detects threats but does not automatically block every finding, and an NLB is not the same HTTP-origin choice.|A WAF web ACL rate-based rule on CloudFront can rate-limit matching request populations at the edge.|Flow Logs provide diagnostics and custom automation, not the direct managed web rate-limiting control.","waf cloudfront", "Rate limiting is one layer of DDoS defense, not a guarantee against every attack. Restrict direct origin bypass and retain capacity/Shield protections as appropriate.")
R(403,"BD","secure","Identity protection","Use workload roles for machine access and MFA for human sign-in, rather than assigning long-lived user keys to hosts.",
"ACM stores/manages certificates, not an AWS API access-key vault.|MFA strengthens supported administrator authentication/session workflows.|An IAM user per EC2 instance creates long-lived credential lifecycle overhead.|An EC2 role provides scoped automatically managed temporary credentials to the workload.|Static access keys on the host create unnecessary storage/rotation/exfiltration risk.","iam")
R(404,"B","secure","Account governance","Control Tower provides a landing zone, account provisioning and baseline controls; Config aggregation alone only observes configurations.",
"OpsCenter is an operations issue workflow, not an account factory/landing-zone provisioner.|Control Tower landing-zone controls and Account Factory standardize eligible account provisioning and baselines.|A Config aggregator observes resource/compliance data but does not by itself provision the accounts and network baseline.|RAM shares supported resources; it does not create organization accounts or their landing zones.","controltower")
R(405,"AE","secure","Client-side encryption","To encrypt before upload, use a client encryption library with KMS-protected or independently managed client master-key material.",
"A suitable client-side library can encrypt locally using data keys protected by a customer-controlled KMS key.|An EC2 login key pair is not an S3 server-side object-encryption option.|A second S3 bucket is not a supported server-side key-management service.|S3-managed SSE keys are not exposed as client-side master keys to the application.|An independently managed client-side master key can encrypt/protect local data keys before upload.","clientside kms", "The source's 'must spend time' is awkward but both choices require deliberate access/key lifecycle management. KMS rotation does not retroactively re-encrypt existing objects.")
FIXES[406] = {"prompt": "An investment bank is launching a digital wallet on EBS-backed EC2 instances, storing logs, transactions and billing statements in S3. Which TWO controls protect the confidentiality of sensitive data stored on those volumes and objects?", "options": ["Create an EBS snapshot.", "Use AWS Shield and WAF.", "Enable Amazon S3 server-side encryption or use client-side encryption.", "Migrate the EC2 instances from a public to a private subnet.", "Enable EBS encryption."]}
R(406,"CE","secure","Encryption at rest","Protect sensitive stored objects/blocks with S3 encryption and EBS encryption, not just backups or perimeter placement.",
"A snapshot is a recovery point, not by itself an encryption/confidentiality control.|Shield and WAF protect network/application ingress rather than encrypt stored content.|Server-side or correctly implemented client-side encryption protects S3 object data.|Private placement narrows network reachability but does not encrypt existing stored blocks or S3 objects.|EBS encryption protects the volume's blocks and associated supported snapshot data using KMS.","ebs sse", "The original screenshot was visually transcribed to restore five options and remove interleaved option text from the prompt. 'Protect' is clarified as confidentiality rather than treating every security control as an encryption answer.")
FIXES[407] = {"option": {2: "In the NACL, allow inbound TCP 443 from 0.0.0.0/0 and outbound TCP ephemeral ports 1024–65535 to 0.0.0.0/0."}}
R(407,"CD","secure","Stateless network filtering","NACLs need inbound service and outbound client ephemeral ports; stateful security groups need the intended inbound application rule.",
"Return packets go to client ephemeral ports, not necessarily destination port 443.|Outbound return permission alone leaves the inbound NACL deny in place.|Allow inbound HTTPS and outbound replies to client ephemeral ports through the stateless NACL.|An inbound HTTPS SG rule permits the client-initiated session, and its replies are tracked statefully.|An outbound HTTPS SG rule does not allow clients to initiate an inbound connection.","vpc", "Editorial correction: the source's 32768–65535 return range covers some clients only. The choice now uses 1024–65535 to cover common client ephemeral ranges; the original screenshot remains available.")
R(408,"D","cost","Cost reporting","Cost Explorer API provides programmatic cost/usage queries and forecasts, including pagination for result sets.",
"Budgets tracks thresholds/plans; SQS is not a native report-delivery replacement for cost query APIs.|Manual CSV download adds operations instead of directly using the programmatic cost/forecast interface.|SNS budget notifications report configured budget conditions, not arbitrary on-demand usage datasets.|Cost Explorer API supports cost/usage and forecasting requests with the relevant filters and pagination.","costapi")
R(409,"BE","secure","DDoS architecture","Dedicated hardware and HPC adapters are not DDoS mitigation mechanisms; edge controls and distributed ingress are.",
"CloudFront's distributed edge network can be part of a supported web DDoS defense, so it is not one of the unsuitable choices.|Dedicated tenancy isolates hosts; it does not block or absorb malicious internet requests.|Shield/WAF provide supported DDoS and application-filtering controls, making this suitable rather than an exclusion.|Distributed load balancing, scaling and a private DB tier improve the architecture's exposure/resilience posture.|EFA targets tightly coupled compute networking and does not filter hostile internet traffic; arbitrary multiple EFAs are also instance-limited.","waf efa")
R(411,"A","resilient","Long-term database backups","Use retained snapshot recovery points for a ninety-day policy; native Aurora automated-backup retention is not ninety days.",
"A supported AWS Backup snapshot plan can retain recovery points for ninety days.|Snapshot export to S3 is not the same complete restorable Aurora snapshot retention workflow, nor automatic as stated.|Aurora's native automated backup retention maximum is thirty-five days, not ninety.|Managed database snapshots cannot be directly downloaded as ordinary files and placed in Glacier this way.","backup pit")
FIXES[412] = {"options": ["Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration", "FTP", "CloudFront Origin Access Control (OAC)", "AWS Direct Connect"]}
R(412,"A","performance","Global transfer performance","Transfer Acceleration optimizes supported long-distance S3 transfer paths through edge locations; it does not guarantee identical speed from every client.",
"Enable and benchmark the accelerated S3 endpoint for geographically distant internet uploads.|FTP is a protocol, not a native global S3 acceleration feature.|OAC authorizes CloudFront origin access; it does not accelerate arbitrary client uploads to S3.|Direct Connect is a provisioned hybrid circuit, not a universal path for public users worldwide.","transferaccel", "The missing FTP option was restored from the screenshot. Geography, file size and client networks determine actual benefit and added cost.")
R(413,"AC","resilient","Archive retrieval capacity","Expedited Flexible Retrieval with provisioned capacity supports urgent retrieval needs; ordinary bulk/select/range choices do not reserve throughput.",
"Expedited retrieval is the low-latency archive restore tier among these options.|Glacier Select is not a capacity reservation or general guaranteed full-object restore solution.|Provisioned retrieval capacity reserves supported expedited request capacity/throughput; buy sufficient units for the workload.|A byte-range request can reduce data read but does not reserve retrieval capacity.|Bulk retrieval is designed for slower inexpensive restores, not the under-fifteen-minute requirement.","s3", "Validate object-size expedited limits, current provisioned-unit throughput/request guarantees and supported archival service/class. Capacity does not create a universal application end-to-end SLA.")
h(414,"Hibernation can preserve application memory, but A (migrate to an enabled instance) and C (enable on an existing supported stopped instance) depend on current eligibility/root-volume configuration. The source gives neither instance/AMI eligibility nor a consistent single choice, and hibernation also bills stored RAM in EBS.","cost","Compute hibernation","hibernate")
h(415,"Tracking new objects, ordinary delete markers and permanent version deletes requires the appropriate ObjectCreated and both relevant ObjectRemoved events (or ObjectRemoved:*). Options B and C each omit one deletion case; the MQ options are not the stated SQS queue. No offered option covers all required events.","resilient","Object events","s3events")

