R(429,"C","performance","Managed stream delivery","Firehose manages streaming delivery to supported storage/analytics destinations, including transformation integrations.",
"DynamoDB Streams captures changes to DynamoDB tables, not arbitrary sensor event ingestion.|SQS is a work queue and does not itself deliver/transform data into all listed destinations.|Firehose buffers, transforms where configured and delivers streaming records to supported destinations.|Redshift is an analytical database, not the general multi-destination ingestion/delivery service.","firehose")
R(430,"D","secure","Restricted SSH ingress","SSH uses TCP port 22; a /32 source restricts the rule to one corporate IPv4 address.",
"UDP is the wrong transport for normal SSH.|The NACL option still specifies the wrong transport, UDP.|A /0 is not a single-host restriction and would admit the entire IPv4 source space.|A TCP 22 SG ingress rule from 175.45.116.100/32 authorizes only the specified address.","vpc", "Also ensure public routing, instance addressing and NACL/host rules permit the connection.")
R(431,"AD","secure","Encryption at rest","S3 server-side encryption and client-side encryption both protect object contents at rest; perimeter defenses and different storage services are not replacements.",
"S3 SSE-S3 provides AES-256 server-side object encryption; SSE-KMS offers additional key controls.|Encrypted EBS snapshots are a different resource, not the required S3 object-encryption method.|Moving data to EBS does not satisfy the stated requirement to store it in S3.|Encrypting before upload protects the stored ciphertext; HTTPS additionally protects transport.|Shield mitigates DDoS exposure rather than encrypting stored object bytes.","sse clientside", "Encryption alone does not establish HIPAA compliance; this question concerns the technical at-rest encryption control.")
