R(433,"B","resilient","Persistent storage lifecycle","DeleteOnTermination controls whether the associated EBS volume is deleted when the instance terminates.",
"Termination protection is not a persistent-volume retention policy and does not cover every automated termination path.|Set the relevant block-device mapping DeleteOnTermination=false in the launch configuration/template.|Suspending health checks weakens recovery and does not define volume lifecycle behavior.|DataSync is not the native control preserving the existing attached root EBS volume on termination.","termination", "Retained volumes still incur charges and need a recovery/cleanup plan; keeping data is not automatically making a new instance use it.")
R(434,"D","resilient","Durable work buffering","Use a durable queue to retain admitted work while consumers scale; adding capacity alone cannot preserve requests already dropped.",
"Larger instances may increase capacity but do not durably retain accepted work during overload.|Placement groups optimize instance proximity, not buffering of pending requests.|Aurora does not configure EC2 scaling or queue web requests automatically.|SQS decouples producers and workers and exposes backlog metrics for scaling consumers.","sqs as", "Use the actual SQS backlog metric, such as ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible or backlog per worker; the source's generic metric label is shorthand. Producers must acknowledge requests only after durable admission.")
R(435,"D","resilient","Hybrid network hub","A Direct Connect gateway associated with Transit Gateway can extend a shared hybrid connection to supported multi-account VPC attachments.",
"Ordinary VPC peering does not transit another VPC's Direct Connect gateway connection.|VPN CloudHub uses VPN connectivity and does not reuse the dedicated circuit as the proposed scalable DX hub.|A separate circuit per account adds cost/operations when supported shared gateway architecture suffices.|The DX gateway/Transit Gateway association provides scalable routed access for eligible VPC/account attachments.","dxgateway peering", "Configure transit/private VIF type, allowed prefixes, route tables, shared attachments and DNS forwarding; the gateways alone do not create directory/DNS resolution rules.")
R(436,"D","resilient","Serverless Kubernetes","EKS provides Kubernetes orchestration and Fargate supplies per-pod isolated compute without customer-managed worker hosts.",
"ECS is not a Kubernetes control plane, so it does not run the existing Kubernetes cluster semantics.|EMR is a data-processing platform, not this microservice container orchestration target.|Outposts/Cluster Autoscaler and AppFlow do not supply the requested no-host-management pod compute model.|EKS with suitable Fargate profiles runs Kubernetes pods on managed isolated compute; configure pod autoscaling separately.","eksfargate", "ECS Service Auto Scaling is not an EKS control. Interpret the source's generic 'Service Auto Scaling' as configuring appropriate Kubernetes HPA/VPA behavior, not an automatic cross-service feature.")
