h(446,"S3 Object Lambda is closed to new customers from November 7, 2025. The question does not establish an eligible existing customer and conflates obtaining a transformed response with avoiding the Lambda function reading the source object. Its bucket/key answer is historical, not a complete current solution.","performance","Object transformation","objectlambda athena")
h(447,"Both ECS Fargate (with its default larger ephemeral allocation) and a container-image Lambda configured with 5 GB of /tmp can satisfy at least 5 GB of serverless temporary storage. Runtime, execution duration and exact-versus-minimum sizing are not specified, so B and D are both viable.","performance","Serverless storage","lambdaStorage fargate")
R(448,"BC","secure","Private content delivery","Protect S3 origin access and CloudFront viewer authorization separately.",
"A custom function adds unnecessary authentication code instead of native signed-viewer controls.|A supported OAI bucket policy can restrict the S3 REST origin to CloudFront in this legacy design.|Signed URLs/cookies grant the selected client time-limited access to the distribution.|Direct S3 presigned URLs bypass the stated CloudFront-only delivery requirement.|Origin Shield improves cache/origin-request efficiency, not viewer authorization.","cloudfront oac", "For new deployments prefer OAC, especially with SSE-KMS or advanced origin features. The source's OAI option requires removing competing public bucket/ACL access.")
R(449,"B","resilient","Active-active DNS","Weighted records with health evaluation can keep multiple healthy regional endpoints active and omit unhealthy ones.",
"Active-passive keeps a standby rather than using all healthy resources concurrently.|Health-aware weighted records distribute active traffic among healthy endpoints.|A passive weighted design does not meet the active use of all available resources.|Primary/secondary terminology is active-passive rather than the requested active-active multi-resource pattern.","routing", "Route 53 has documented behavior when all resources are unhealthy; DNS routing is not a hard guarantee no failing endpoint is ever returned.")
R(450,"B","secure","Organization guardrails","An OU-level SCP can deny protected Config modification actions to member-account principals, including their root users.",
"A detective rule notices changes after the fact and does not prevent deletion.|An inherited SCP deny on the developer OU prevents specified protected Config management actions.|IAM users do not have attachable trust relationships that supply this guardrail.|A role trust policy governs role assumption; it does not remove the member account root user's own permissions.","scp", "Scope the deny and maintenance exceptions so trusted deployment/security roles can manage required controls. SCPs do not constrain the organization management account itself.")
R(451,"C","secure","Restricted SSH ingress","An instance security group must allow inbound TCP 22 from the administrator's actual source address.",
"NACLs are associated with subnets rather than a single VPC-wide NACL; the instance SG is the direct listed fix.|TCP 3389 is RDP, not the SSH service port.|Permit SSH TCP 22 from the trusted source IP with a narrow CIDR.|DLM schedules snapshots; it does not authorize SSH network traffic.","vpc", "Also check key/user name, routes, public addressing and NACL return ports; successful access to another host does not prove this host's path is identical.")
R(453,"B","performance","Scalable application data","DynamoDB supplies flexible keyed records and AppSync supplies a managed application API with real-time integration capabilities.",
"AppFlow integrates SaaS data rather than providing the voting application's mobile API.|AppSync and DynamoDB fit managed scalable keyed vote records and application access.|Aurora is relational and Cognito authenticates users; this is not the closest flexible-document API pair.|RDS and MQ add relational/broker components rather than the directly suitable managed keyed API/database pair.","dynamo appsync", "A flexible item schema does not remove the need to design keys/indexes, idempotent vote admission and an efficient ranking aggregation model.")
R(454,"A","resilient","Multi-AZ compute","One regional load balancer with an Auto Scaling group across multiple AZs avoids placing all web capacity in one AZ.",
"Two AZs in one Region provide a supported regional load-balancer/ASG topology with redundancy.|All eight servers in one AZ share that AZ's failure boundary.|One regional load balancer/ASG does not span four Regions as asserted.|A single regional ELB does not front two Regions in this manner.","as alb", "Maintain enough spare capacity for the required AZ-loss load and configure replacement health checks; four surviving instances may not serve an eight-instance workload without scaling.")
R(455,"A","performance","Speech analytics","Use managed speech-to-text, text translation and sentiment APIs rather than training a custom model.",
"Transcribe produces text, Translate normalizes supported languages to English, and Comprehend evaluates sentiment.|Polly synthesizes speech, Rekognition analyzes visual data and Fraud Detector is not a sentiment model pipeline.|Comprehend does not transcribe audio and Kendra/Detective do not perform the asserted translation/sentiment roles.|Lex is a conversational service and Clarify is model explainability/fairness tooling, not this managed sentiment sequence.","transcribe translate sentiment", "Check language/region support and input-format limits for each service; preserve timestamps and translation provenance if needed.")
R(456,"D","cost","Storage lifecycle","S3 Lifecycle transitions retained objects into appropriate lower-cost archive classes according to age/rules.",
"Timestream is a time-series database, not an S3 object storage-class scheduler.|An EC2 cron worker adds operational overhead for a built-in bucket lifecycle feature.|SQS queues messages rather than changing S3 object storage classes.|Lifecycle transition rules perform managed age-based movement to supported archive classes.","s3", "Objects remain in S3 when their storage class changes. Set archive timing, minimum durations and retention/expiration according to actual access needs.")

R(457,"A","secure","Tag compliance","Config required-tags-style evaluation identifies missing required metadata on supported resources.",
"A Config managed/custom rule can evaluate the supported resource types for required tags.|A custom scheduled Lambda duplicates the supported managed rule mechanism and adds maintenance.|Tag policies standardize supported tag values but do not make an S3 file of names a missing-tag detector.|SCPs authorize/deny API requests; they do not run a configuration inventory scan.","config", "A required-tags rule checks presence/allowed values; a stricter naming convention may need a custom rule. Some resource types are not supported by every managed rule.")
h(458,"Only C explicitly configures DAX and provisioned auto scaling. A falsely assumes console-style auto-scaling defaults for a CLI-created table; B adds unrequired cross-Region replication/cost and does not fix missing capacity configuration. The source does not establish TWO required cost-effective choices.","performance","Database scaling","dynamoauto")
R(459,"C","secure","VPC peering","VPC peering is non-transitive: DEV-to-UAT and UAT-to-PROD do not create DEV-to-PROD routing.",
"Overlapping CIDRs prevent the normal direct peering design rather than enabling it.|Peering through UAT does not act as transit routing between the other two VPCs.|Create a direct DEV/PROD peering connection and authorize both routes/security controls.|A route cannot use another pair's peering connection as a transitive path.","peering")
R(460,"CD","resilient","Instance lifecycle","An EBS-backed instance stop/start may change hosts and discards attached instance-store contents; ENI/EIP associations normally persist.",
"An associated allocated EIP normally remains associated across ordinary stop/start.|Instance-store data loss and possible host replacement mean the system does change.|A stop/start can place the instance on different underlying hardware.|Instance-store data is lost on stop; retain important data on persistent storage/backups.|An existing instance's ENI is not routinely detached by a normal stop/start.","ec2billing publicip", "This assumes an EBS-backed instance with attached instance-store devices. Instance-store-backed root instances cannot be stopped in the same way.")
R(461,"A","performance","Stream consumers","Lambda event source mappings read Kinesis records in batches and checkpoint processing.",
"A Kinesis stream with a Lambda mapping supports managed batched record consumption.|S3 plus Spectrum queries stored objects rather than reading live stream record batches.|Firehose can invoke a transform Lambda on delivery batches, but it is not the same consumer read interface for a data stream asked here.|Athena queries S3 datasets, not the live stream through Lambda polling.","kinesis esm", "This answers the batched-stream question; adding analytics does not itself resolve the original overloaded web server or prevent 503s.")
h(462,"Current Lambda uses shared Hyperplane ENIs, not one ENI per invocation. IP exhaustion and ENI quota errors have distinct failure codes; EC2ThrottledException points to throttled EC2 operations rather than proving either duplicate IP-exhaustion option. Exact error/context is needed for two justified causes.","resilient","VPC function troubleshooting","lambda")
FIXES[463] = {"prompt": "A Lambda function reads documents that were client-side encrypted using a customer-managed KMS key and stored in FSx for NetApp ONTAP. After processing, it writes results to S3. Which permission configuration allows the function to decrypt the document data keys?"}
R(463,"D","secure","KMS workload authorization","The execution role is the AWS principal making SDK calls. Authorize that role through the applicable identity/key policy model.",
"The role permission is relevant, but the Lambda function ARN is not the role principal to grant key use.|A Lambda resource policy controls invocation, not the function code's KMS calls.|A resource-policy ARN is not the calling execution-role principal.|Grant the required decrypt operation to the execution role and ensure the KMS key policy permits that use.","lambda kmspolicy", "Editorial clarification: this is client-side document encryption. FSx-managed at-rest encryption is transparently handled by the service and does not by itself require file-reading code to call kms:Decrypt.")
h(465,"The upload is a search result for a university society website, not an AWS exam question. It contains no answer options and is retained only as a source attachment.","resilient","Non-question attachment","dr")
h(468,"The upload is a Google Drive file-open error page, not readable question content. No question or answer options can be recovered from this image.","resilient","Unreadable source","dr")
