R(522,"A","performance","Log analytics","ALB access logs land in S3 and Athena queries those files with SQL without dedicated analysis servers.",
"S3 provides the supported log destination and Athena queries the retained datasets.|DynamoDB is not the standard direct ALB access-log delivery destination.|A custom EC2 log parser adds hosts/code when serverless Athena meets the analysis need.|EC2/EBS couples durable log storage and analysis to managed hosts unnecessarily.","athena alb")
R(526,"A","secure","Least-privilege user groups","Use department groups with least-privilege policies and explicit MFA-condition denies for protected operations.",
"Groups centralize user policies; a carefully constructed explicit deny can enforce MFA for required operations.|A boundary is a permission ceiling, not a group-based grant or complete MFA policy.|Roles are not attached to IAM groups as policy documents.|SCPs attach to organization entities, not directly to IAM users, and are not user trust policies.","groups iam", "A missing MFA context needs correct condition handling and bootstrap exceptions so users can register/manage MFA. Test federated/long-term-key cases separately.")
R(531,"A","performance","Text sentiment analytics","Use Comprehend for sentiment extraction and OpenSearch Dashboards for the indexed transcript/results visualization.",
"Managed sentiment analysis plus OpenSearch indexing/dashboards supplies the requested no-custom-model pipeline.|Training a custom NLP model adds model lifecycle work not required for supported sentiment analysis.|Textract extracts text from documents/images; the inputs are already transcript text and it does not perform sentiment classification.|Managed Grafana is not the direct native OpenSearch transcript-search dashboard choice presented here.","sentiment", "Extract the transcript text from its JSON wrapper and conform to Comprehend language/size/input-format requirements before running analysis.")
R(532,"D","cost","Short-lived object storage","S3 Standard has no minimum storage-duration charge, unlike the listed IA/archive classes.",
"Standard-IA has a thirty-day minimum duration and retrieval/minimum-object charges.|One Zone-IA also has a thirty-day minimum duration and single-AZ tradeoffs.|Deep Archive imposes a much longer minimum storage duration and restore delays.|Standard avoids an early-deletion minimum-duration penalty for twelve-hour objects.","s3", "S3 Lifecycle expiration is day-based/asynchronous, not an exact twelve-hour deletion scheduler; use suitable scheduling when precise deletion timing is required.")
R(533,"B","resilient","Origin failover","CloudFront origin groups can fail over supported requests between separately configured primary/secondary origins.",
"Lambda@Edge functions are event handlers, not normal origin-group origin endpoints.|Two eligible regional origins in different AZs provide a secondary target for a configured origin group.|S3 cannot execute arbitrary EC2 dynamic application code merely by being an origin.|An Auto Scaling group identifier is not itself a CloudFront origin hostname; a suitable ALB can be an origin.","cferror cloudfront", "Origin failover is limited to supported methods/status conditions and does not replicate application state. For general dynamic writes, design appropriate regional load balancing/recovery.")
R(534,"B","secure","Key custody choices","CloudHSM provides dedicated customer-controlled HSMs; KMS supplies a more abstract managed key service with supported dedicated-HSM integration options.",
"The operational and custody models are materially different.|Dedicated HSM control can be the reason to choose CloudHSM when its specific cryptographic/integration requirements apply.|The described low-operations managed-key need normally points to KMS, not administering CloudHSM clusters.|Payment processing does not universally require CloudHSM; match the actual validated compliance and key-custody requirements.","cloudhsm kms", "KMS also uses protected validated HSM infrastructure and supports custom key stores; do not equate managed KMS with unprotected software keys.")
FIXES[535] = {"prompt": "A company runs a supported RDS for MySQL database and wants a managed cross-Region read architecture whose replication is typically sub-second. Which option is the closest fit, without treating typical lag as a guaranteed SLA?"}
R(535,"A","performance","Cross-Region database reads","Aurora Global Database is the purpose-built low-lag managed cross-Region architecture; typical lag is not a hard upper bound.",
"Use a compatible Aurora architecture with appropriate cross-Region replication, preferably Global Database for its dedicated replication design.|An engine upgrade alone does not create a replica near remote readers.|RDS MySQL cross-Region asynchronous replicas do not supply a strict sub-second lag guarantee.|A cache can accelerate selected reads but is not the specified managed cross-Region database replication mechanism.","aurora dr", "Editorial update removes the unsupported MySQL 5.6 example and the implied guaranteed '<1 second'. Aurora replication can lag; monitor and test the chosen engine/topology.")
R(536,"B","resilient","HTTP function ingress","A Lambda function URL provides a direct HTTPS invocation endpoint without creating an API Gateway solely as a proxy.",
"API Gateway is valid when its richer routing/auth/throttling features are required, but adds a separate API resource here.|A function URL provides the direct webhook HTTPS endpoint with the required authorization/application validation.|A queue URL is not an arbitrary HTTP POST webhook that transparently invokes Lambda with the third party's payload.|A custom EC2 proxy adds servers and management for a natively supported endpoint.","functionurl", "Configure compatible authentication or application signature verification. A public NONE URL is not acceptable solely because the payload contains sensitive data; apply the actual access requirements.")
R(538,"C","cost","Non-production availability","Remove optional test/development standby costs before weakening highly utilized production compute or production database availability.",
"Interruptible capacity may disrupt the busy production servers.|Replacing utilized reserved discounts with On-Demand can increase cost.|Where non-production requirements permit, single-AZ test/development RDS removes standby cost without changing production Multi-AZ.|Removing the ELB damages production traffic distribution/availability.","rds savings")
R(539,"CE","resilient","Database availability","Traditional RDS Multi-AZ improves durability and failover availability within one Region; it is not cross-Region replication or read scaling.",
"Multi-AZ does not automatically rewrite or optimize SQL.|The synchronous standby is in another AZ of the same Region, not another Region.|A healthy standby protects availability/durability against eligible primary component/AZ failures.|A traditional standby is not a general performance/read capacity addition.|Supported maintenance can use failover to reduce disruption compared with a single-instance deployment.","rds", "The question's opening asks for multiple Regions, which Multi-AZ alone cannot provide. These answers describe its actual within-Region benefits only.")
R(540,"B","cost","Capacity assurance","On-Demand Capacity Reservations reserve matching zonal capacity; regional RIs supply discounts rather than a specific-AZ capacity guarantee.",
"Regional RIs do not reserve capacity in a selected AZ.|Use matching On-Demand compute backed by explicitly configured zonal Capacity Reservations for capacity assurance.|Dedicated Hosts fit tenancy/licensing needs, not a stated requirement for ordinary zonal batch capacity.|Ordinary Capacity Reservations do not natively imply an automatically recurring nightly reservation schedule.","capacity ri", "The source's recurring-schedule implication is incorrect: automate reservation scheduling/cancellation where appropriate or use supported capacity reservation features and account for idle reserved-capacity charges.")
R(541,"B","resilient","Application logs","Beanstalk application bundles are stored in S3 and logs can be streamed to CloudWatch or bundled/published to S3.",
"Logs are not confined to the instance EBS volume; managed retrieval/streaming options exist.|Beanstalk uses S3 application versions and supports appropriate S3 log bundles and CloudWatch log streaming.|Direct Glacier log delivery is not the stated ordinary Beanstalk logging mechanism.|CloudTrail audits AWS API activity rather than storing arbitrary web-server application log files.","beanstalk cloudwatch")
R(542,"B","performance","Traffic distribution","Cross-zone load balancing lets eligible load balancer nodes distribute requests to targets across enabled AZs.",
"Direct Connect SiteLink connects external sites, not application target balancing.|Cross-zone behavior controls whether a node can distribute to targets in other enabled AZs.|Path rules select target groups by URL path, not balance capacity across AZs.|IPAM manages address allocations rather than live request distribution.","alb", "Defaults/configurability vary by load balancer family and target-group settings; equal request counts do not imply equal processing load.")
R(543,"B","secure","Cross-account object access","For legacy ACL-enabled buckets, require bucket-owner-full-control on uploads so the bucket owner receives full control.",
"CORS controls browsers and does not transfer object permissions.|A bucket policy can reject uploads lacking the bucket-owner-full-control canned ACL in the legacy ownership model.|Requester Pays affects billing, not who controls uploaded objects.|Access logging is unrelated and an arbitrary caller IAM policy is not the bucket-side upload enforcement rule.","s3ownership", "For modern buckets prefer Bucket owner enforced Object Ownership, which disables ACLs and gives the bucket owner ownership. Full-control ACL grants and ownership transfer are distinct concepts.")
R(544,"B","performance","Conversational interfaces","Lex V2 models intents, slots and conversation flow with Lambda fulfillment/code hooks.",
"Comprehend provides text analysis, not the complete managed conversational intent/slot/fulfillment service.|Lex supports the text conversation and invokes configured Lambda hooks for business actions.|Polly synthesizes speech; SSML does not supply chatbot intent orchestration.|Rekognition analyzes visual content, not text chatbot intent and fulfillment.","lex")
R(545,"C","secure","Workload IAM roles","EC2 application SDK calls should use a scoped instance role instead of stored long-lived access keys.",
"Encrypting static keys locally retains a key-delivery/rotation problem.|A web root is especially inappropriate for credential storage and long-lived secrets.|Assign an IAM role through the instance profile so the SDK obtains temporary authorized credentials.|Glacier is archive storage, not a runtime credential-issuing service.","iam metadata")
R(546,"C","secure","IPv6 egress","An egress-only Internet Gateway permits instance-initiated IPv6 traffic and its replies while blocking unsolicited inbound internet sessions.",
"A NAT instance is not the native IPv6 egress-only gateway control.|A conventional NAT gateway's NAT44/NAT64 roles differ from direct IPv6 egress-only routing.|Route the intended IPv6 internet destinations to an egress-only IGW for outbound-only stateful connectivity.|An ordinary IGW is not itself the dedicated unsolicited-inbound-blocking IPv6 feature.","ipv6egress", "Return packets for allowed outbound connections are inbound IPv6 traffic; the feature blocks unsolicited initiation, not all replies.")
R(547,"A","secure","Organization guardrails","Organizations SCPs set permission ceilings on member-account users/roles; identity/resource policies still supply grants.",
"Use organization/OUs and scoped inherited SCPs for common service/action guardrails.|Cross-account access connects identities/resources but does not create a centrally enforced organization permission ceiling.|Federation supplies identity sessions, not the organization-wide authorization ceiling by itself.|An ordinary IAM policy is not automatically applied across every independent account.","scp")
