R(55,"D","resilient","Recovery strategies","Pilot light minimizes steady compute while retaining core data/services so the remaining application can be launched during recovery.",
"Active-active retains more live capacity and replication complexity than the limited-budget requirement suggests.|Warm standby keeps a functioning reduced application and normally has higher standing cost than pilot light.|Backup/restore usually has more restore/provisioning work than the intended minutes-level recovery pattern.|Pilot light fits a low-standing-cost, minutes-oriented recovery strategy with replicated core state and automated scale-out.","dr", "A twenty-minute objective is not guaranteed by the strategy name. Benchmark replication lag, launch time, quotas and the full recovery process.")
FIXES[76] = {"option": {2: "Use API Gateway private integration through a VPC Link to an appropriate private load balancer/backend, restricting backend access to the authorized path."}}
